    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0133" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg59"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d40-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Aboard The</hi> H.M.S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps">Duke of
                                York</hi>”</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-22"
                            >December 22, 1941</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following for President from “Rejoined”
                        Naval Person.</p>
                <p>Impossible to reach mouth of Potomac before 6.30. p.m. E.S.T. which would be too
                    late for plan you have so kindly made for us.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d40-f2"/> Can
                    anchor Hampton Roads Gate 4.15 p.m. E.S.T.</p>
                <p>I should like to come on by aircraft to Washington Airfield reaching you in time
                    for dinner.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d40-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>If weather prevents this could I have a train to Washington from whatever is most
                    convenient starting point in the vicinity of Hampton Roads?</p>
                <p>Please on no account come out to meet me either way. Looking forward so much to
                    seeing you at the White House.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d40-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d40-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Halifax and delivered by the British Embassy to the White House.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d40-f2" n="2" xml:id="d40-f2-content">
                <p>No copy has been found of a telegram from Roosevelt to Churchill containing “the
                    plan”, but Churchill (<hi rendition="#italic">The Grand Alliance</hi>, p. 662)
                    says that it “had been intended that we should steam up the Potomac and motor to
                    the White House.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d40-f3" n="3" xml:id="d40-f3-content">
                <p>Arrangements were made for Churchill and his party to fly from Hampton Roads to
                    Washington, arriving on the evening of December 22.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
